# Line endings. Hashed and byte-compared files (the packaged records and tables, the saved-form fixtures and goldens,
# the reference arrays) keep the bytes the repository holds on every platform: git on Windows ships with
# core.autocrlf=true, which writes a text file out with CRLF, so a pinned sha256 of the file no longer matched.
# One rule for every text file rather than a list of data folders, so a new folder is covered without anyone
# remembering it (tests/test_gitattributes.py fails if a tracked file is left out); the exceptions are the binaries,
# which git must never touch.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.npz binary
*.npy binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.whl binary
*.usdc binary
*.usdz binary
